From 92c452b54089449b281adff1f81c88d8776607ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 01:32:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): refuse waterjet posting until the jet records
 exist

The post gate refuses each unsuppressed waterjet operation by name. The
refusal names the missing standoff height, jet on/off records, pierce
dwell records and waterjet laws (#1882, #1885). A user post that serves
waterjet goes through the same gate and writes no file.

The stock simulation skips waterjet operations and refuses its verdict
by name, so the post gate shows a visible not-judged line. The nozzle no
longer enters the dexel model as a cutter.

The waterjet clause adds nothing when the program list cannot be read:
the sim clause already refuses with that reason.

The path notes say that jet and dwell records are not implemented, and
name a pierce on the kerf ring at zero lead-in. The page shows the same
consequence, drops the G-code words from the compensation choice and
gives each tab row its own name.

Fixes #3637

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
